            "effect": "ignored:block_threads",
            "rationale": {
              "text": "With N=4096 and 1024 threads per block, each thread handles exactly 4 elements. 1024 threads = 32 warps fills a block completely and maximises warp-level reduction efficiency (warp shuffles cover all 32 warps). Given only 32 rows, having maximum intra-block parallelism is critical to saturate the SM. This is the maximum legal block size on this hardware.",
              "lang": "en"
            }
          }
        ]
